<p>The <code>{ignore}{barcode}{/ignore}</code> tag writes EAN-13, EAN-8, UPC-A and Code 128 barcodes
as inline SVG - sharp at any size and on paper, no font, no image library. A scanner or a
phone reads them straight from the screen.</p>

<h2>Products - EAN-13</h2>

<table>
  <tr><th>Product</th><th>Barcode</th></tr>
  {products}
  <tr>
    <td>{$name}</td>
    <td>{barcode $ean, height=50}</td>
  </tr>
  {/products}
</table>

<p><code>{ignore}{barcode $ean, height=50}{/ignore}</code> - twelve or thirteen digits are an EAN-13;
given without its check digit, the tag adds it.</p>

<h2>A shipping label - Code 128</h2>

<div class="label">
  <strong>PAD Demo Shop</strong><br>
  Parcel {$parcel}<br>
  {barcode $parcel, height=70}
</div>

<p><code>{ignore}{barcode $parcel, height=70}{/ignore}</code> - letters, digits and punctuation;
runs of digits are packed two to a symbol.</p>

<h2>The other types</h2>

<table>
  <tr><th>Type</th><th>Barcode</th><th>Tag</th></tr>
  <tr>
    <td>EAN-8</td>
    <td>{barcode '9638507', type='ean8'}</td>
    <td><code>{ignore}{barcode '9638507', type='ean8'}{/ignore}</code></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>UPC-A</td>
    <td>{barcode '03600029145', type='upca'}</td>
    <td><code>{ignore}{barcode '03600029145', type='upca'}{/ignore}</code></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Bars only, in colour</td>
    <td>{barcode 'PAD', height=30, scale=3, plain, color='#2e7d32'}</td>
    <td><code>{ignore}{barcode 'PAD', height=30, scale=3, plain, color='#2e7d32'}{/ignore}</code></td>
  </tr>
</table>
